# Flat Pose Diagnostics at 5 FPS

This notebook checks why the single-mouse model did not clearly improve pose
metrics over the dense triplet model. The key rule is that both checkpoints are
evaluated on the same held-out source windows and the same mouse indices.

## Diagnostic Contract

```text
Dense checkpoint: checkpoints/flat_dense_triplet_5fps/flat_best.pt
Single checkpoint: checkpoints/flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps/flat_best.pt
Window: 16 observed frames -> 24 predicted frames
Rate: 5 FPS
Default sample: 30 triplet windows = 90 paired mouse cases
Seeds: 42, 43, 44
Output: outputs/evaluations/pose_diagnostics_5fps/results.jsonl
Per-case rows: outputs/evaluations/pose_diagnostics_5fps/cases.jsonl
```

The diagnostics report:

- matched autoregressive metrics for both variants
- teacher-forced metrics to separate one-step prediction quality from rollout drift
- single-minus-dense paired deltas and single-model win rates
- low/medium/high motion slices from the same selected mouse windows
- Gaussian calibration from sampled bivariate distributions
- dense-triplet attention mass split into within-mouse and cross-mouse context

## Run Diagnostics

```sh
python src/diagnostics.py --config src/config/test__flat_pose_diagnostics_5fps.yml
```

## Reprint Latest Tables

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from diagnostics import print_pose_diagnostics

result_path = repo_root / "outputs/evaluations/pose_diagnostics_5fps/results.jsonl"
record = json.loads(result_path.read_text().splitlines()[-1])
print_pose_diagnostics(record)
```

## Inspect Worst Relative-Ordering Cases

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

case_path = repo_root / "outputs/evaluations/pose_diagnostics_5fps/cases.jsonl"
rows = [json.loads(line) for line in case_path.read_text().splitlines()]
single_rows = [
    row for row in rows
    if row["model"] == "single_mouse" and row["mode"] == "autoregressive"
]
single_rows = sorted(
    single_rows,
    key=lambda row: row["metrics"]["relative_ordering_error"],
    reverse=True,
)

for row in single_rows[:10]:
    print(
        row["sequence_id"],
        "start=", row["start_frame"],
        "mouse=", row["mouse_index"],
        "seed=", row["seed"],
        "motion=", row["motion_group"],
        "ROE=", round(row["metrics"]["relative_ordering_error"], 4),
        "BLE=", round(row["metrics"]["bone_length_error_px"], 3),
        "SOE=", round(row["metrics"]["skeleton_orientation_error_deg"], 3),
    )
```
